
The Process of hiding the complex implementation from the user and providing
the necessary functionality to the user is known as Abstraction


Real World Example

Braking Mechanism of the Car only necessary functionality is provided to the user to apply the brake 

how it works internally when we apply the brake all the complex implementtion is hidden from the user 
this is what the example of Abstraction


In Java Abstraction can be achieved in 2 ways 

//   partial abstraction can be achieved using the method overriding 


1. using Abstract class we can provide the astraction to the parent class methods and new implementation will be provided in the child class 
and given with the reference of the parent (at runtime it will execute the child class overriden method (but if someone from middleware try to see the implementation then it will show the abstract method ))
